The bug arises from the incorrect handling of the byte order for the GUID structure. The original implementation used a mixed-endian representation where some components were stored in little-endian format while others were in big-endian format. This inconsistency led to incorrect comparisons and representations of GUIDs, particularly when converting from text to the internal structure and when outputting the GUIDs as strings. The EFI specification requires a specific byte order, and the failure to adhere to this resulted in the observed issues.

